<title>UK: Shell sees Texaco deal announcement in Q1.</title>
<headline>Shell sees Texaco deal announcement in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil giant Royal Dutch/Shell Group said on Thursday it expects to make an announcement in 1997's first quarter on its plans to merge its U.S. downstream operations with Texaco Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;I would expect an announcement in the first quarter,&quot; said Cor Herkstroeter, Royal Dutch chairman and head of the Shell group's committee of managing directors.</p>
<p>Herkstroeter told journalists he was &quot;confident&quot; that an agreement would be reached.</p>
<p>Oil giants Shell and Texaco first announced their U.S. downstream link-up plans on October 7.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
